eted":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nreproducible godot 4.6 stable\n\n### System information\n\nwindows 11, godot 4.6 stable\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen I define any Joint axis rotation (even only one) in any IK chain the end bone will never match the target node but will follow it with an offset. I am assuming that IK is calculating the angles as if the constraints are not defined but then applying the angles with the constraints.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nin the scene I have added a JacobianIK3D to a rigged 3d model of a robot arm. Defined start and end bones and attached a marker3D as the target.\n\nWithout any Joint axis defined, the end bone will follow the target correctly\n<img width=\"1593\" height=\"852\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/365c8400-325a-4267-af10-704ed35069dd\" />\n\nIf I define a joint axis, the end bone will have an offset to the target. If i move the target, the bones move aswell, but always with that offset.\n\n<img width=\"1593\" height=\"876\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c72bfce7-c3fd-47bd-81a5-03e5ef0f57e0\" />\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[ik-joint-offset.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25160537/ik-joint-offset.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url